# Task 7b: gaps in TeaVM's code generator (G7-nan-compare, G7-negative-zero, G7-joining) and one in its
# classlib stubs (G7-suppress-warnings). Written from the pinned JDK's observed output, the public Javadoc
# (SuppressWarnings, java.lang.annotation.Annotation) and TeaVM's own source, which it changes (clean room,
# D14); no OpenJDK source was opened.
#
# NaN comparisons. javac compiles a < b on doubles as dcmpg + ifge, and a > b as dcmpl + ifle; the two
# differ only for NaN (dcmpg gives 1, dcmpl -1). ProgramParser turned both into the same COMPARE, and the
# AST optimizer fused compare(a, b) >= 0 into a >= b, so NaN < 1 came out true. Now:
#   - COMPARE of floats and doubles means fcmpg/dcmpg (NaN gives 1, as GlobalValueNumbering already
#     folds it), and fcmpl/dcmpl become -compare(b, a), which is equal for every input;
#   - OptimizingVisitor fuses compare(a, b) > 0 as !(a <= b) and >= 0 as !(a < b), and fuses through
#     the negation with the operator mirrored, so fcmpl/dcmpl still compile to one f64 comparison;
#   - ExprOptimizer.invert and the Wasm generator's branch negation no longer turn !(a < b) into
#     a >= b for floats (only == and != swap); the rest are wrapped in NOT / i32.eqz;
#   - WasmRuntime.compare, used when a comparison is not fused, gives 1 for NaN instead of 0.
# Negative zero: NEGATE of a float or double compiled to 0 - x, which is +0.0 for x = 0.0; it is now
# f32.neg / f64.neg. Both fixes reach javac's and TeaVM's own constant folding only when compiler.wasm is
# itself compiled by the patched TeaVM, which teavm-javac-0105 arranges: "double z = -0.0" is folded by
# javac, and n < 1 with n = 0.0 / 0.0 by GlobalValueNumbering, both inside compiler.wasm. Do not ship
# this patch without 0105: with the stock-compiled GlobalValueNumbering, the new fcmpl/dcmpl form folds
# NaN < 0 as true, and "" + 0.0 / 0 printed -0.0 (the fork-no-0105 build shows it on G-primitives).
#
# Collectors. WasmGCClassGenerator.getEnumConstantsFunctionOffset() returned the offset without laying
# out java.lang.Class first, unlike the other Class offsets, so it was still -1 when the first use came
# before anything else touched Class: "Field index must be >= 0" for Collectors.toList(), joining(),
# groupingBy() and counting() (all build an EnumSet of Characteristics) in a program whose main is an
# instance void main(). Reproduced with TeaVM on the JVM, where a static main compiled and an instance
# void main() did not.
#
# @SuppressWarnings. TSuppressWarnings had no value() element, so javac said "cannot find symbol: method
# value()" and then crashed. The Javadoc gives it String[] value(). teavm-javac-0104 fixes the other half
# (java.lang.annotation.Annotation extended itself in the compile classlib).
#
# No earlier patch touches ProgramParser, OptimizingVisitor, ExprOptimizer, WasmRuntime,
# WasmGCClassGenerator or TSuppressWarnings. BaseWasmGenerationVisitor is also changed by teavm-0009, far
# from these hunks, so each applies with the other left out.
#
# Applies to: github.com/konsoletyper/teavm tag 0.13.1 (b3a245b7)

